# Git Safety Rule (Highest Priority)

This rule overrides every other instruction.

## Never touch main/master

Under NO circumstances:

- push to `main` or `master`
- merge into `main` or `master`
- force push to protected branches
- delete or rewrite history of `main`/`master`

Even if asked to "push everything", do **not** push those branches.

## Always work on a separate branch

Before code changes:

1. Check current branch
2. If on `main`/`master`, create and switch immediately

Names: `feature/<name>`, `fix/<name>`, `refactor/<topic>`, `chore/<topic>`, `docs/<topic>`

Never continue development on `main` or `master`.

## Commits

Commit frequently with conventional messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `chore:`).

## Pushing & PRs

- Only push the feature branch: `git push origin <feature-branch>`
- Never push `main`/`master`
- Open a PR from the feature branch; **never merge automatically** — wait for user approval

## Destructive commands — require explicit permission

`git push origin main|master`, `--force`, `--force-with-lease`, `--mirror`, `reset --hard`, `rebase -i`, `branch -D`, `clean -fd`

## Before every git operation

Verify current branch, target branch, remote, and working tree. If target is `main`/`master`, **STOP** and ask.
